Imagine a software license stating:\
\
*You may never decompile this program under any circumstances.*\
\
Now imagine a developer performing decompilation that satisfies Article 6.\
\
The contractual prohibition cannot extinguish that statutory permission. The conflicting restriction is void.\
\
And Article 8 goes further: it also protects specified rights to make necessary backup copies and to observe, study, or test a program's operation. \
\
**This is a real example of legislation protecting computational activities against conflicting contractual restrictions.**\
