### United States: DMCA \'a71201(f)\
\
The United States has a related, though different, provision.\
\
Under [17 U.S.C. \'a71201(f)](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/1201), someone lawfully entitled to use a computer program may, under specified conditions, circumvent access controls to identify elements necessary for interoperability with independently developed software.\
